{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplicity of a Graded Module.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplicity of a Graded Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multiplicity of a graded module multiplicity of a graded module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplicity of a Graded Module.md","fileName":"Multiplicity of a Graded Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multiplicity of a Graded Module","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:15\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Regular Sequences and Syzygies]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","Hilbert Polynomial","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplicity of a Graded Module.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplicity of a Graded Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multiplicity of a graded module multiplicity of a graded module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplicity of a Graded Module.md","fileName":"Multiplicity of a Graded Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multiplicity of a Graded Module","heading":"Multiplicity of a Graded Module","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For a non-Artinian finitely generated graded module M of dimension d, its multiplicity is obtained from the leading coefficient of its [[Hilbert Polynomial]] after multiplying by (d−1)!.\n\nMultiplicity measures the leading rate of graded growth rather than the full Hilbert function. The associative formula decomposes it into contributions from top-dimensional prime components.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","Hilbert Polynomial","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplicity of a Graded Module.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplicity of